# Keep the payload byte-identical whichever OS checks it out.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites every text
# file to CRLF on checkout. That breaks two things at once: tools/install.sh
# stops running ("bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M"), and every payload
# file installed from a Windows clone reports DIFFERS forever against one
# installed from macOS or Linux, because the installers compare bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf
